      "text": "**Paris-Rouen 1894**: Considered the first organized motor race, though it was billed as a \"reliability trial\" (concours des voitures sans chevaux -- contest of horseless carriages). 25 vehicles started; 21 finished the 126km course. First across the line: Count Jules-Albert de Dion (steam-powered vehicle) -- disqualified because his steam car required a stoker (not \"autonomous\"). Actual winners: Peugeot and Panhard-Levassor petrol vehicles."
    },
