      "text": "EARLY ERA CHAMPIONS/CARS:\n  1950-51: Alfa Romeo (158/159) dominance\n  1952-53: Ferrari 500 (Alberto Ascari 2x champion)\n  1954-55: Mercedes W196 (Fangio -- dominant)\n  After 1955 Le Mans disaster: Mercedes withdraws\n  1958-60: Cooper rear-engine revolution\n           Before: engine in front (tradition)\n           Cooper T51: engine behind driver\n           Better weight distribution, handling\n           Every team adopts within 2 years\n```"
