      "text": "GROUND EFFECT (1977-1982):\n  Colin Chapman (Team Lotus): genius lateral thinker\n  KEY INSIGHT: Car body as inverted wing\n  Lotus 78 (1977): sidepods shaped as venturi tunnels\n    -- Underfloor suction creates massive downforce\n    -- No drag penalty (unlike wing downforce)\n    -- Car effectively \"sucks\" itself to track\n  Lotus 79 (1978): refined ground effect\n    -- Mario Andretti dominates, wins championship\n  PROBLEM: Ground effect extremely sensitive to height\n    -- Car rides 5mm from ground\n    -- Any bump = massive downforce loss = accident\n    -- Several serious accidents\n    -- Flat-bottom rule introduced 1983: BANNED"
    },
