      "text": "MODERN ERA INNOVATIONS:\n  1997  McLaren MP4/12: Mercedes Illmor carbon fibre\n        brake calipers\n  1998  Grooved tyres introduced (reduce cornering speed)\n  2003  Launch control and traction control re-banned\n  2009  KERS (Kinetic Energy Recovery System):\n        Stores braking energy, deploys as extra power\n        (~80bhp for 6.7 sec per lap)\n        Early reliability issues; became universal\n  2011  DRS (Drag Reduction System):\n        Rear wing flap opens on straights to reduce drag\n        Only in designated zones; increases overtaking\n  2014  Hybrid power unit era begins:\n        1.6L V6 turbo + MGU-H (heat recovery) + MGU-K\n        Total output: ~1,000bhp\n        Thermal efficiency: ~50%+ (road cars ~30-35%)\n        Mercedes dominance: 8 consecutive constructors\n        titles (2014-2021)\n  2017  \"Halo\" cockpit protection device introduced\n  2022  Ground effect returns: new regulations allow\n        underfloor aerodynamics within new safety framework\n        (porpoising problem initially)\n```"
